{"wrong":"very agree","fix":"strongly agree","why":"'Very' cannot directly modify a verb."}
{"wrong":"this restaurant food","fix":"this restaurant's food","why":"Use the possessive to identify food belonging to this restaurant."}
{"wrong":"than","fix":"as","why":"Use 'as', not 'than', after 'not so good'."}

{"wrong":"very agree","fix":"totally agree","why":"Use 'totally', not 'very', to modify 'agree'."}
{"wrong":"this restaurant food","fix":"this restaurant's food","why":"Use the possessive form to refer to the restaurant's food."}
{"wrong":"not so good than","fix":"not as good as","why":"Use 'as good as' for this comparison."}

{"wrong":"There was a lot of people","fix":"There were a lot of people","why":"Plural “people” takes “were,” not “was.”"}
{"wrong":"everyone become","fix":"everyone became","why":"Past-tense narration requires “became.”"}
{"wrong":"a really fun experience","fix":"really fun experience","why":"“Fun” is an uncountable adjective here, so omit “a.”"}
